se we have to  cooperate and on climate change and on  everything else we you know we we live  in the same planet and we have to try  and find a way of of living with people  but i think that the process of these  vast meetings and the lead-up to them  and the the desire to extract  concessions has led us to  sometimes be somewhat uh inadequate in  the way we talk about other issues  and  i therefore think that it'd be much  better to get away from these vast  annual meetings with uh  i'm sorry to say futile outputs because  they are futile uh seen from outside by  ordinary people  these are talking shops that produce  pieces of paper these aren't where the  action happens and you know the the  improvements have come from technology  not from policy ninety percent of them i  would say  [Music]  you
 

